  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a 5% thermal-testing limit but allow a six-year compliance period for pre-adoption models and do not require automatic market exclusion above 5%, which substantially weakens S2 for Northwind. S5 retains a mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall trigger with no transition, directly exposing Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S3 and S4 settle at acceptable six-year retrofit and 36-month suppression deadlines, while S1 imposes strict 24-hour incident reporting."
